  "slug": "john-dodson-judge",
  "summary": "Sir John Dodson (1780–1858) was an English civil lawyer, judge, and Tory MP. Educated at Merchant Taylors’ School and Oriel College, Oxford, he became an advocate at Doctors’ Commons in 1808 and edited Admiralty reports. He represented Rye in Parliament from 1819 to 1823.\n\nDodson served as Admiralty Advocate from 1829 to 1834 and King’s Advocate from 1834 to 1852. Knighted in 1834, he later became master of the faculties and vicar-general to the Archbishop of Canterbury. From 1852 he was judge of the Prerogative Court of Canterbury; he also served as Dean of the Arches until his death. He was sworn into the Privy Council in 1852.\n\nHis legal publications include reports of cases in the High Court of Admiralty, issued between 1811 and 1822. He married Frances-Priscilla Pearson in 1822. Their only son, John George Dodson, became an MP and was created Lord Monk Bretton in 1884.",
